> This is the **style contract** the `backend-engineer` and
> `frontend-engineer` agents read before writing code. Its whole purpose is
> to make new code look like the code already here. It describes **what the
> codebase does**, not what some architecture says it should do. The live
> code always wins — if this file drifts from reality, fix the file.

## How this file is used

- Read by every coding agent in its pre-task ritual (alongside `brain-hot.md`).
- Generated/refreshed by `/onboard` from sampling real files — not hand-prescribed.
- Organized **per area → per aspect**. Keep each entry to an observed fact +
  (optionally) a one-line example path. No aspirational rules.

